(Scheduling assumptions) Tj
0 -13 Td
(A context switch consumes simulated CPU time and is charged only when changing processes.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(The initial dispatch after idle does not incur a context switch. Arrivals during a switch are admitted.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(Tier 2 is non-preemptive: a running Tier 2 process completes before another choice is made.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(Effective priority = max\(0, initial priority - floor\(Tier 2 waiting / aging interval\)\).) Tj
